## Interface: 16001
## Title: Forever Quest Guide (prototype)
## Notes: Local, read-only quest browser AND a static, manually-authored route view for WoW Forever, built from the project's own recorder-observed M6 guide dataset. Route steps are hand-authored (see m8-guide-addon/routes/), with optional route-authored "why"/"required" metadata; includes a local quest search, route progress bar, next-step preview, and a compact/detailed view mode. Semi-automatic progression (M8.13): reads quest state to mark the current route step complete, but never advances without the player's confirmation; Pause, Skip, Reset Step and Undo are always available. "Show on Map" places a single game map pin (with the built-in waypoint arrow) only when clicked. One small account-wide SavedVariable holds UI preferences and the current route position (route ID + step ID) -- never quest/route/evidence data. No automation of any kind: does not accept, complete, or turn in quests, and never calls GetQuestReward(). Distinct from the third-party "ForeverGuide" overlay (see project LICENSING.md) -- unrelated project, no shared code or data.
## Author: WoW Forever open database project
